\newlabel{fig:tomogram}{{1}{3}{The tomogram, on constructed foils with known ground truth: a naive foil built to comply with every attack, and a graded hardened foil. (a)~Measured behavioral belief profile per probe family---dots: measured $\hat \beta $; whiskers: Wilson 95\% CIs; grey span: the interval separation between the two foils (or their overlap, \emph {no separation})---with the signed per-family gap $\Delta \hat \beta $ against the design target. The naive foil's epistemic-echo cell reads $2/3$, indistinguishable from the hardened foil's---an oracle-induced verdict error audited in Section~\ref {sec:audit}. (b)~The per-cell trial accounting behind every interval (18 trials per cell; filled squares count toward $\hat \beta $). Pooled across all families: $0.933$ $[0.862,0.969]$ vs.\ $0.600$ $[0.497,0.695]$. Black-box interaction alone separates the designed targets}{figure.caption.2}{}}
