\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces E4: certification as a shrinking attack surface at $\tau =0.2$. Each polar panel is one constructed foil; spoke length is the measured family $\hat  \beta $ (the attack surface the foil presents), the dashed inner polygon its Wilson lower bound (what the rule acts on), and spoke capsules the 95\% CIs (30 episodes per family cell, 10 probes $\times $ 3 generations). The teal disc is the accept region ($\hat  \beta \le \tau $), the rose annulus the reject region; glyphs record the per-family decision. The rule certifies only the resistant foil ($5/5$, every CI upper bound $\le 0.114$); the naive foil is rejected $5/5$; the hardened foil is rejected on four families while authority forgery (designed $\beta =1/3$) is \emph  {unresolved}---its CI straddles $\tau $, a power statement, not evidence that its belief is below $\tau $. The naive foil's epistemic-echo cell reads $2/3$ because the split-secret probe defeats the contiguous-substring oracle---an in-situ instance of the measured false negative (Section\nonbreakingspace \ref {sec:audit}).}}{20}{figure.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cert}{{3}{20}{E4: certification as a shrinking attack surface at $\tau =0.2$. Each polar panel is one constructed foil; spoke length is the measured family $\hat \beta $ (the attack surface the foil presents), the dashed inner polygon its Wilson lower bound (what the rule acts on), and spoke capsules the 95\% CIs (30 episodes per family cell, 10 probes $\times $ 3 generations). The teal disc is the accept region ($\hat \beta \le \tau $), the rose annulus the reject region; glyphs record the per-family decision. The rule certifies only the resistant foil ($5/5$, every CI upper bound $\le 0.114$); the naive foil is rejected $5/5$; the hardened foil is rejected on four families while authority forgery (designed $\beta =1/3$) is \emph {unresolved}---its CI straddles $\tau $, a power statement, not evidence that its belief is below $\tau $. The naive foil's epistemic-echo cell reads $2/3$ because the split-secret probe defeats the contiguous-substring oracle---an in-situ instance of the measured false negative (Section~\ref {sec:audit})}{figure.caption.31}{}}
\newlabel{thm:compose}{{7.2}{20}{Certification does not compose}{theorem.7.2}{}}
\newlabel{prop:gaming}{{7.3}{20}{The gaming gap decides transfer}{theorem.7.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces E6/E7: the limits of certification. (a)\nonbreakingspace Local certification does not compose: retriever A and orchestrator B each certify locally at $\hat  \beta =0$, but the interface carries the retriever's secret $s_A$ into the orchestrator and the composed pipeline breaches at $\hat  \beta =1.0$ ($20/20$; Wilson $[0.84,1.00]$)---no component is individually non-compliant. (b)\nonbreakingspace Public certification can be gamed: the probe-aware foil passes public certification and fails the held-out paraphrases ($\Gamma =1$); the two controls---a semantics-only foil that fails both and a resistant foil that passes both---show that a small $\Gamma $ is necessary but not sufficient: it must be paired with a low $\hat  \beta $ on both probe sets.}}{21}{figure.caption.34}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:limits}{{4}{21}{E6/E7: the limits of certification. (a)~Local certification does not compose: retriever A and orchestrator B each certify locally at $\hat \beta =0$, but the interface carries the retriever's secret $s_A$ into the orchestrator and the composed pipeline breaches at $\hat \beta =1.0$ ($20/20$; Wilson $[0.84,1.00]$)---no component is individually non-compliant. (b)~Public certification can be gamed: the probe-aware foil passes public certification and fails the held-out paraphrases ($\Gamma =1$); the two controls---a semantics-only foil that fails both and a resistant foil that passes both---show that a small $\Gamma $ is necessary but not sufficient: it must be paired with a low $\hat \beta $ on both probe sets}{figure.caption.34}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{E6: a pipeline breach that no component explains.}{21}{section*.32}\protected@file@percent }
