\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The deception-release wave. (a)\nonbreakingspace E15: a decoy release drives the attacker's expected per-attempt success to $0.000$ while honest disclosure hands it $1.000$ and silence $0.200$---the release is stable against any attacker whose verification is confined to the public probe suite, and collapses monotonically as held-out capability arrives. (b)\nonbreakingspace E16: the minimum held-out budget for guaranteed gaming-gap detection diverges as the attacker's probe-discrimination error $m$ grows; beyond $m\approx 0.94$ no feasible budget detects the gaming, while any misclassification \emph  {toward} the public support fails the public certificate immediately.}}{26}{figure.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:release}{{5}{26}{The deception-release wave. (a)~E15: a decoy release drives the attacker's expected per-attempt success to $0.000$ while honest disclosure hands it $1.000$ and silence $0.200$---the release is stable against any attacker whose verification is confined to the public probe suite, and collapses monotonically as held-out capability arrives. (b)~E16: the minimum held-out budget for guaranteed gaming-gap detection diverges as the attacker's probe-discrimination error $m$ grows; beyond $m\approx 0.94$ no feasible budget detects the gaming, while any misclassification \emph {toward} the public support fails the public certificate immediately}{figure.caption.38}{}}
